      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T20:47:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pushing on this. I traced the Chromium side: the landed integration is chromium/src CL 8164520, where IcoRustImageDecoder inherits SkiaImageDecoderBase and therefore depends on getFrameCount/getFrameInfo. The open CL 8257029 only prepares an A/B trial; it does not introduce the adapter discussed in the previous Skia review.\n\nI revised this patch accordingly rather than relying on an unfinished migration: getEmbeddedImage* is removed, the existing frame API remains the supported Chromium path, entries are ordered like Blink’s legacy ICO decoder, and a nonzero frame index now selects the requested entry and decodes its native rect into SkiaImageDecoderBase’s full-canvas buffer. Frame zero retains dimension-based selection for existing SkCodec callers. The new test covers regular and incremental decoding with exactly that Blink allocation pattern.\n\nI agree that selection and indexed decoding were being conflated. This patch now keeps indexed decoding and uses the existing frame metadata for selection; any future ICO-specific API should arrive together with a concrete Chromium consumer rather than speculatively in Skia.",
      "parentUuid": "f3c4b712_0ccec5a6",
      "revId": "2dbc7a08e103d0c4ba4a8a7eed22cc50748a256c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3c4b712_0ccec5a6",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T17:51:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How can I learn about the plan for using these from Chromium?  I am just trying to double-check that this will all work in the long term.  Maybe just seeing corresponding Chromium-side changes would help us get confident in the direction we are taking here?\n\nAnd if you have a plan that you are confident in, then this is probably all that matters.  I am asking some questions below to help check that the plan is okay, but ultimately you probably are more familiar with this area than me at this point.\n\nSome specific questions / observations::\n\n* I assume that going forward we won\u0027t be able to use `blink::SkiaImageDecoderBase` (because it relies on `getFrameCount` / `getFrameInfo`).  At least not its `::Decode` method (but maybe we would still be able to reuse some helpers).  Hopefully we can avoid some of that complexity (around color space transformations for example).\n* I see that the legacy decoder\u0027s `blink::ICOImageDecoder::Decode` takes a frame `index` (well, image `index`).  So it seems that a lets-decode-specific-frame-index API fits okay on Blink side, right?\n* Maybe the animation-frames-based-decoding-API is okay as long as there is also **additional** API for finding the right frame index?  Maybe the root problem [in the previous CL discussion](https://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/1328756/12#message-051fbfad75184496b5ffff3997defb2ad8c4c9dd) wasn\u0027t the decoding API, but using the decoding API for selecting the frame to decode?",
